<Base
  title="About"
  description="Meet Ty and the working garage behind Garage Sidequests."
>
  <article class="reading">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON AT THE BENCH</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Ty.</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I spend an unreasonable amount of time taking hardware that probably
        should have been left alone and figuring out what else it can do.
      </p>
      <p>
        Garage Sidequests is where I document those projects: homelabs,
        networking, electronics, automation, hardware reuse, 3D printing, and
        whatever technical rabbit hole looks interesting next.
      </p>
      <h2>There is no clean-room lab here.</h2>
      <p>
        It’s a working garage, a couple of 3D printers, a pile of hardware, and
        usually more than one project happening at the same time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sometimes things work. Sometimes they break. Usually another side quest
        starts somewhere in between.
      </p>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about a project or something worth exploring?{" "}
        <a href="mailto:hello@garagesidequests.com">
          hello@garagesidequests.com
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
